Z||000002||Formula88||08-23-2001||01:13 PM||||I LOVE it!  The cam phasing and variable displacement, and variable intake manifold are GM's versions of the VTEC on Hondas.  I always wondered what would happen if you actually built a REAL engine with superior technology.  Well, now we know.  So, Acura gets 200HP out of 2.0 Litres.  Big, fat, hairy, deal.  GM gets 750HP out of 7.5L!  It's the same specific output, but with a real engine!<P>Archie?  Chris?  Jay?  You guys payin' attention?  Hell, I'd even settle for an automatic with one of these suckers.....<P>------------------<BR>"God made us brothers.  Prozac made us friends." :D||||reg||10
Z||000003||artherd||08-23-2001||02:01 PM||||Yay!  I just mentioned in another thread that there is no reason a modern engine shouldn't make 100bhp a litre, looks like GM finally did something about it :)<P>Exactly, who cares if your 1.6 litre makes 100bhp/litre.   Now, you start talking about a 4.6 litre engine with that kind of efficency.....   :) :) :)<P>Still, the stupid deactication crap dosen't work in automotive engines, peroid. It didn't work for GM (remenber the 8-6-4?) and even in Mercedes newest V12s, it's lurchy.  <P>About time GM finally made 100bhp/litre in an engine that matters, but really, 100bhp/litre isn't all that impressive anymore.  It's expected, and many are doing it withought GDI.  Ferrari is pushing 110bhp/litre (in a 3.6l engine...  for 398bhp. the 360 has torque too.) Honda's S2000 dosen't, but it's making nearly 120bhp/litre.<P> These are volume production cars also, not prototypes.<P>Still, it's about time, let's hope they bring this to market (sans the stupid deactivation junk) *soon* !!! <P>PS: that V12 makes 405lb-ft at 1500rpm. I do belive that's quite a bit more than a corvette's peak :)<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||DRH||08-23-2001||02:09 PM||||Wow.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> 90% of it's torque at 1500 RPM. With 450 ft lbs of torque and 750 HP that means the peak HP must be AT LEAST at 8753 RPMs (HP = Torque * RPM / 5252). That's if it still had 450 ft lbs at 8753. Realistically it'll be even higher.<P>An engine that pulls hard from 1500 to 9000+ RPM??? Who needs a transmission!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||14
